                  {
                    "at": "around Africa",
                    "places": [
                      {
                        "name": "Cape of Good Hope"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then, in 1869, a French-led company opened a canal straight through Egypt, linking Port Said on the Mediterranean to the city of Suez on the Red Sea.",
          "shots": [
            {
              "type": "ai_image",
              "at": 0,
              "prompt": "19th century oil painting of steamships entering a newly opened canal in the desert, flags and crowds on the banks",
