    {
      "title": "Who Controls the Canal",
      "mood": "tension",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "In 1888, the major powers signed an agreement that promised free passage to every ship, in war and in peace.",
          "shots": [
            {
              "type": "quote",
              "at": 0,
              "quote": "The Suez Maritime Canal shall always be free and open, in time of war as in time of peace, to every vessel of commerce or of war, without distinction of flag.",
              "author": "Convention of Constantinople, 1888"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But in 1956, Egypt's president, Gamal Abdel Nasser, nationalized the canal company, partly to pay for a huge new dam on the Nile.",
          "shots": [
            {
              "type": "title_card",
              "at": 0,
              "on_screen_text": "1956",
              "subtitle": "The canal company is nationalized"
            },
            {
              "type": "map",
              "at": "dam",
              "map": {
                "steps": [
                  {
                    "focus": [
                      "Egypt"
                    ],
                    "places": [
                      {
                        "name": "Aswan High Dam"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain, France and Israel invaded. Pressure from the United States and the Soviet Union soon forced them to withdraw.",
